mainmenu "YakoGL Slint cluster sample"

config SLINT_WINDOW_WIDTH
	int "Window width in pixels"
	default 1024
	range 320 4096
	help
	  The window the cluster renders into and the screen shows. The
	  default is the AM62P's panel, which the other panels also fit; a
	  board whose panel is larger sets its own size in its conf so the
	  picture fills the panel (the Verdin iMX8MP's DSI panel: 1280x800).
	  The UI scales with the window (ui/layout.slint's unit).

config SLINT_WINDOW_HEIGHT
	int "Window height in pixels"
	default 600
	range 200 4096

config SLINT_WINDOW_BUFFERS
	int "Windows the cluster is rendered into in turn"
	default 1
	range 1 3
	help
	  One where the board layer copies or pans the window (the AM62P,
	  the Pi 4). Two or three where the screen flips to the window by
	  address and scans it in place (the i.MX8MP at its panel's size):
	  the frame being drawn is then never the one the LCDIF scans, no
	  copy is made, and the show's wait for the latch paces the frames
	  at the panel's rate. Each window is a full buffer of the board
	  layer's (the i.MX8MP: the GPU carve-out).

config SLINT_ANIMATE_FOREVER
	bool "Animate until the board is reset (ignore YAKOGL_BOARD_ANIMATE_S)"
	help
	  For a power-on demo that has to keep running (the iMX8MP route-3
	  image): the run never reaches its result records, its hold or its
	  reset. Pair it with a watchdog that is fed for as long as the
	  loop is alive (the iMX8MP: GC_BOARD_WDOG_UNBOUNDED).

config SLINT_FRAME_REPORT
	bool "Route 3 measurement: where each frame's time goes, on the timeline UART"
	depends on YAKOGL_BOARD_IMX8MP_ROUTE3
	select YAKOGL_BOARD_IMX8MP_ROUTE3_REPORT_LINE
	help
	  Every 120 frames, three lines on the timeline UART (alias
	  yakogl-timeline-uart, tl-uart1.overlay; else the console UART),
	  written by the board layer's lowest-priority report thread: A53F,
	  the frame's draw, GPU, show and swap times; A53G, the GL entry
	  points' CPU time and the Rust side's phases (set_vehicle, timers,
	  render); A53Y, YakoGL's draw steps and the GPU's cycle counters.
	  A measurement: off, the sample neither times its phases nor prints
	  them, and the report thread does not exist.

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
